      ],
      "text": "**Possibly a little better, but don’t count on the haze clearing.** For Sunday, October 18, Singapore’s forecast wind shift and showers may reduce smoke drifting in from Kalimantan, but haze from Sumatra could still reach the island. NEA has not yet posted its 24-hour PSI forecast for Sunday; its latest forecast for today, Saturday, is **PSI 150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nCheck NEA’s 24-hour PSI forecast later today before planning outdoor activities; for conditions right now, check the 1-hour PM2.5 readings. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
